# The binary naturals' constructors restored where a numeral is written in β normal form:
# `λz e o. o h`, the β normal form of `binary_odd h`, is in one
# class with `binary_odd h`, and `λz e o. e h` with `binary_even h`, so that a back end that reads the constructors'
# applications (narrow-blocks' literals) reads such a numeral, and nothing in the host recognizes the shape. This is
# the reverse β that restores a noinline function where its unfolded shape appears, written as one lemma per constructor with a field; binary_zero needs none, its β normal form being its
# own body.
#
# Sound by δ and β alone: binary_odd is `λh _ _ o. o h` and binary_even `λh _ e _. e h` (library binary/natural), so
# each left side contracts to its right side in one β step after δ, inside ⊢_{βη} (CONTRIBUTING.md, "Terms").
#
# Termination, derived and not proved: an instance read right to left adds the application of a constructor to a class
# the match already had; read left to right it adds the thunk that the β rule adds as well. Neither side's match
# creates a node the other side matches anew, so the instances are at most the thunks of the two codes and the
# constructors' applications in the input graph.
#
# Measured 2026-11-19 by a probe kept out of the tree, set_free_sum_small_direct through the rounds of contest-entries-wren with this module
# added to the first: the class of the numeral 13 gains `binary_odd` applied to the class of 6, the extraction writes
# every numeral as the constructors applied, and the program's one narrow block compiles; without it the block is
# refused, "a literal does not decode".
λ export
. (λtuple. tuple λmixin. mixin mixin)
λ omega
. omega (omega (omega (omega corpora "library") "binary") "natural")
λ _ binary_even binary_odd _ _
. export
λ _ rewriting _ _
. rewriting
λ _ lemmas _
. lemmas
  ( λ s
    . s (λk. k "binary_odd_restored") (λh. binary_odd h) (λh z e o. o h) λ_ md _. md λk. k "[β](docs/design/gezi-set-equations-proofs.md)"
  + λ s
    . s (λk. k "binary_even_restored") (λh. binary_even h) (λh z e o. e h) λ_ md _. md λk. k "[β](docs/design/gezi-set-equations-proofs.md)"
  )
